w","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.lean#L255-L265"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">instance</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.html#BitVec.instMul\"><span class=\"name\">BitVec</span>.<span class=\"name\">instMul</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Mul\">Mul</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#BitVec\">BitVec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.html#BitVec.instMul","kind":"instance","line":253,"name":"BitVec.instMul","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.lean#L253-L253"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.html#BitVec.mul\"><span class=\"name\">BitVec</span>.<span class=\"name\">mul</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#BitVec\">BitVec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#BitVec\">BitVec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Multiplies two bitvectors. This can be interpreted as either signed or unsigned multiplication\nmodulo `2^n`. Usually accessed via the `*` operator.\n\nSMT-LIB name: `bvmul`.","docLink":"./Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.html#BitVec.mul","kind":"def","line":245,"name":"BitVec.mul","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.lean#L245-L252"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.html#BitVec.abs\"><span class=\"name\">BitVec</span>.<span class=\"name\">abs</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#BitVec\">BitVec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#BitVec\">BitVec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the absolute value of a signed bitvector.","docLink":"./Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.html#BitVec.abs","kind":"def","line":239,"name":"BitVec.abs","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.lean#L239-L243"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">instance</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/BitVec/Basic.html#BitVec.instNeg\"><span class=\"name\">BitVec</span>.<span class=\"name\">instNeg</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Neg\">Neg</